{"title":"2005 IMO Shortlist Problems/G3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/G3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Ukraine</i>)\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/1/5a1788ec6ad85848dbaeacf2cea3bf65bc2fef76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle ABCD$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> be a parallelogram.  A variable line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> passing through the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/734ef645c78704dbe5a136258a49d8425298f623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle A$\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" /> intersects the rays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/9/999a25b627b5ddfe0a6af29e0d4b635adc2cc483.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle BC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cd146a95812ea4c4d41073cfdab0c3500337927.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle DC$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b47736949a2a26fa60c778fc69b1a281d43b3a75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle X$\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/4/d547c9ed7793c8e2979684d0228219d9e95b7ad0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle Y$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />, respectively.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/3/3c31f3404a91311bb4be7cec9d49bb510d592d34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle K$\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/1/bf1e3168ff93ce6ae8adc13c43870dcee9c0b2e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle L$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> be the centres of the excircles of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e2f4f765e57e62e37f2d693c1c544e057dfa5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle ABX$\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/5/d5585fbc4513e7664461365c45591482f7fa80a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle ADY$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, touching the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/6/2267cc49c40b0d57b141a7da793504f9d8beaa92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle BX$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/d/88d824a063bfafddf88a4b0960bec16e448194db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle DY$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />, respectively.  Prove that the size of angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27d35a18719fceea94ea42e7f304fff601385a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle KCL$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> does not depend on the choice of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><i>This was also Problem 3 of the 2006 3rd German TST, and a problem at the 2006 India IMO Training Camp.  It also appeared in modified form as Problem 3, Day 3 of the 2006 Iran TST.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/G3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70ba0a73459ee8a2b688b214dea935cf2ba8c669.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_1, \\ell_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> be the interior angle bisectors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/a/fda6dde5dea7386535d082ea004f87eb86ac4926.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle ABX, YAD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/d/5fd98db3c32da3429e2ce1e895bb433d59ba05ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle m_1, m_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"11\" /> be the exterior angle bisectors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/9/5a9cb5ad033e8d8881b1b2b185cd4363fd31403e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle ABC, CDA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/3/3c31f3404a91311bb4be7cec9d49bb510d592d34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle K$\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" /> is the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c871230b42d36fc6b151f00b6ef32fc5dae2d2a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_1, m_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/1/bf1e3168ff93ce6ae8adc13c43870dcee9c0b2e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle L$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> is the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/c/f3ca2aa18bfce4cdb88b0d47ea49d24d7fb07d70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_2, m_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<center> <span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:ISL2005G3.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/e/e9/ISL2005G3.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"496\" height=\"240\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span> </center>\n<p>Let us denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5b3c1e7b8eee4d386e329521027373c9db51308.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" /> as the measures of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/a/44aa7728ecd02668a4e2d72d82abced472d68986.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAK, \\angle LAD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"119\" height=\"16\" />, and denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/6/266e35f5321957d58fc1cbef4306703c2bf75bde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\alpha = x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/a/41aa966de0d1dc0c0699c142108b93bfe91bbf6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAD \\equiv \\angle DCB \\equiv 2 \\alpha$\" width=\"182\" height=\"13\" />.  Furthermore, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/0/da092a7d0f138325cb5a717eb8e3bd8b16987a11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle BK$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> is the exterior angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/4/f94bd9d7a26cd1112d46cfcebde46607448791e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle ABC$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, we know that the exterior angle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/4/1d4c88760d9d2c9f8bbd70affce86bcf65470ae9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle ABK$\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/6/266e35f5321957d58fc1cbef4306703c2bf75bde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\alpha = x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/1/081ddd4f8c50b0b942c62f315b5d0264432b0366.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AKB \\equiv y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" />.  Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b2033dba59025eb95d7639b4a7c3f04e662722.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ALD \\equiv x$\" width=\"88\" height=\"13\" />.  It follows that triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/7/0e77dc8d6c85e12d20a9e6a8e6e8b0e42b211d6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle ABK, LDA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" /> are similar.  Then since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/1/5a1788ec6ad85848dbaeacf2cea3bf65bc2fef76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle ABCD$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> is a parallelogram,\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/0/f30aba751f2221332e08ca67ed82a109b6dcb5f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BK}{DC} = \\frac{BK}{AB} = \\frac{DA}{LD} = \\frac{CB}{LD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"208\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Since we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f7ecca64440c9d353c5364c04f8ebf4bf31b4ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle KBC \\equiv \\angle CDL \\equiv \\alpha$\" width=\"173\" height=\"12\" />, this implies that triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/5/7852d2aeb1f89cb4010dd085f3f0c3c802921281.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle KBC, CDL$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" /> are similar.  This means that\n</p>\n<center> <br />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3e0744b75068ee58f4c87a5e458a2be43ddd46f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle KCL \\equiv 2\\pi - (\\angle LCD + \\angle DCB + \\angle BCK) \\equiv 2\\pi - [(\\angle CBK + \\angle BCK) + \\angle DCB]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"660\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/3/5a329c89dfbd69332c4e1412eac8cd2cefd359ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\equiv 2\\pi - [ (\\pi- \\alpha) + 2\\alpha] \\equiv \\pi - \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"242\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p>\n</center> <p><br />\n</p><p>which is independent of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" />, since  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/7/41745e18c1d8f48f052e396eae97bc8db739704f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\alpha$\" width=\"11\" height=\"8\" /> is always half the measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/5/cb55dc9c50a80e1d9eb23fe53e45f464c0ac755e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />.  <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:Halmos&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:Halmos (page does not exist)\">Template:Halmos</a>\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/G3&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/G3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Shortlist_Problems\" title=\"2005 IMO Shortlist Problems\">2005 IMO Shortlist Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Germany_TST_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 Germany TST Problems (page does not exist)\">2006 Germany TST Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Iran_TST_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 Iran TST Problems (page does not exist)\">2006 Iran TST Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMOTC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 IMOTC Problems (page does not exist)\">2006 IMOTC Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=512720#512720\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=498848#498848\">More Discussion</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018034536\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.074 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 234/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 373/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7617/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    9.059      1 -total\n 69.98%    6.339      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n 27.78%    2.517      1 Template:Halmos\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5027:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018034536 and revision id 15243. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}